<title>INDIA: India's foreign debt falls to $92.6 bln in March.</title>
<headline>India's foreign debt falls to $92.6 bln in March.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's external debt fell to $92.6 billion in March, down from its peak of $99 billion in March last year, and hitting its lowest level since 1993, Finance Minister P.Chidamabaram said.  </p>
<p>&quot;The debt servicing ratio also showed a declining trend,&quot; said a government statement summarising Chidambaram's remarks to a parliamentary committee. He did not give details.</p>
<p>--New Delhi newsroom, +91-11-301 2024</p>
